=== Unsuccessful candidacies ===
There were also four candidates rejected by the [[Portuguese Constitutional Court]] for not complying with the legal requirement of being proposed by 7500 voters:
* Pedro Maria Braga;
* Maria Teresa Lameiro;
* Josué Rodrigues Pedro;
* [[Manuel João Vieira]];

These four candidates were present in the draw of the ballot position, but did not appear in the final ballot.

=== Declined ===

* [[Aníbal Cavaco Silva]] – former [[Prime Minister of Portugal|Prime Minister]] (1985–1995); presidential candidate in [[1996 Portuguese presidential election|the previous election]];<ref name=":0">{{Cite web |date=2000-01-15 |title=Candidato presidencial do PSD |url=https://arquivos.rtp.pt/conteudos/candidato-presidencial-do-psd/ |access-date=2025-12-27 |language=pt-PT}}</ref>
* [[Basílio Horta]] – minister in previous governments; candidate in the [[1991 Portuguese presidential election|1991 presidential election]];<ref>{{Cite web |date=2000-03-25 |title=Perfil de Basílio Horta |url=https://arquivos.rtp.pt/conteudos/perfil-de-basilio-horta/ |access-date=2025-12-27 |website=RTP Arquivos |language=pt-PT}}</ref>
* Daniel Proença de Carvalho – former Minister of Social Communication (1978–1979);<ref>{{Cite web |date=2000-01-19 |title=Candidatura Presidencial do PSD |url=https://arquivos.rtp.pt/conteudos/candidatura-presidencial-do-psd/ |access-date=2025-12-27 |website=RTP Arquivos |language=pt-PT}}</ref>
* [[Diogo Freitas do Amaral]] – former [[President of the CDS – People's Party|President of the CDS]] (1974–1983; 1988–1992); candidate in the [[1986 Portuguese presidential election|1986 presidential election]];<ref name=":CDS01">{{Cite web |title=Estratégia do CDS-PP para as Presidenciais |url=https://arquivos.rtp.pt/conteudos/estrategia-do-cds-pp-para-as-presidenciais/ |access-date=2025-12-27 |language=pt-PT}}</ref>
* [[Francisco Pinto Balsemão]] – former [[Prime Minister of Portugal|Prime Minister]] (1981–1983); former [[President of the Social Democratic Party (Portugal)|President of the Social Democratic Party]] (1980–1983);<ref name=":0" />
* [[José Manuel Barroso|José Manuel Durão Barroso]] – incumbent [[President of the Social Democratic Party (Portugal)|President of the Social Democratic Party]] (1999–2004);<ref name=":0" />
* José Vieira de Carvalho – incumbent Mayor of [[Maia, Portugal|Maia]] (1970–1974; 1979–2002);<ref>{{Cite web |date=2000-01-07 |title=Declarações de Vieira de Carvalho |url=https://arquivos.rtp.pt/conteudos/declaracoes-de-vieira-de-carvalho-2/ |access-date=2025-12-27 |website=RTP Arquivos |language=pt-PT}}</ref>
* [[Marcelo Rebelo de Sousa]] – former [[President of the Social Democratic Party (Portugal)|President of the Social Democratic Party]] (1996–1999).<ref name=":0" />

==Campaign period==
===Issues===
With Jorge Sampaio's re-election practically guaranteed, the campaign was mostly dominated by foreign policy.<ref name="rtp">{{cite news |url=https://www.rtp.pt/noticias/politica/sampaio-e-o-discurso-do-dialogo-e-da-estabilidade_n1706493 |title=Sampaio e o discurso do diálogo e da estabilidade |language=pt |work=RTP| date=29 December 2025 |access-date=9 July 2026}}</ref> In the aftermath of the [[Kosovo war]], Portuguese troops participated in [[NATO]] missions, but the death of a soldier who returned from one of these missions raised suspicions of contamination by [[depleted uranium]].<ref name="rtp" /><ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.publico.pt/2001/01/05/politica/noticia/autopsia-de-hugo-paulino-compativel-com-efeitos-do-uranio-5851 |title=Autópsia de Hugo Paulino «compatível» com efeitos do urânio |language=pt |work=Público| date=5 January 2001 |access-date=9 July 2026}}</ref> The then-socialist government, led by [[António Guterres]], acknowledged that it knew of NATO's use of depleted uranium weapons against Kosovo, and claimed the danger was downplayed.<ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.publico.pt/2001/01/08/politica/noticia/governo-portugues-sabia-do-uso-de-uranio-empobrecido-no-kosovo-6155 |title=Governo português sabia do uso de urânio empobrecido no Kosovo |language=pt |work=Público| date=8 January 2001 |access-date=9 July 2026}}</ref> This case caused an embarrassment to Sampaio's campaign, with his opponents accusing the President of "protecting" the government.<ref name="rtp" />

